==German==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|tolmetsche|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|sla|de}} language; cf. {{proto|Slavic|title=Common Slavic|tъlmačь|interpreter|lang=}} (Russian {{term|sc=Cyrl|толмач|tr=tolmáč|lang=ru}}, Polish {{term|tłumacz|lang=pl}}), whence borrowed from a {{etyl|trk|de}} language; cf. {{proto|Turkic|tilmaç|title=Common Turkic|lang=}} (Turkish {{term|dil|lang=tr}}, Azeri {{term|til|lang=az}}).

===Noun===
'''Dolmetscher''' ''m'' (''pl'' Dolmetscher) '''Dolmetscherin''' ''f''

# [[interpreter]] (as opposed to [[Übersetzer]] ([[translator]]))

